  "theorem": "For every unordered pair i<j, fixing the other 77 coordinate inequalities at their lower endpoints leaves the exact segment B(t)=A+t(E_ij+E_ji), 0<=t<=-2A_ij. Throughout the segment the absolute off-diagonal row sums do not exceed s, so B(t) is PSD. For 0<t<-2A_ij irreducible diagonal dominance is strict in two rows; at the sign-flipped endpoint the signed complete graph is unbalanced. Hence every t>0 is positive definite. These 66 bounded edges plus the 12 diagonal rays form the complete coordinate-edge star at A.",
